t(9, 55, """a strategic one, in his ancient historical alliance with all the forces of evil in the world .. This alliance will fall completely and be struck with destruction .. This is the sign of the Smoke .. It will destroy all his alliances and make those who allied with him for hundreds of years say to him: “Everything is over, everything is lost; we and they (the Muslims) have become equal in strength, and if they are brave and we are cowards, we are finished” .. That is why they come to Sham with 960 thousand soldiers, and their commander orders all the ships burned and tells them: “Either you win or you die” .. Yet this will not change the outcome of their defeat, by Allah's leave .. The problem with the sign of the Smoke is that it has many consequences .. Unfortunately those who speak of it focus only on its environmental consequences .. its technological consequences .. and its punitive consequences, insisting that it is merely a divine punishment on the earth to discipline people and make them admit they were wrong .. Whereas yes, it is a punishment for the disbelievers and the disobedient Muslims, no doubt about that, but it also has many strategic dimensions, intertwined, interlocking and not superficial, and it has terrifying, enormous political and geopolitical effects during the year, month and week of the Dajjal's rule. When the Dajjal emerges he will present himself to the world as a king, claiming first and foremost “lordship of kingship” and not full lordship, and he will install himself as ruler of the world, master of a state and an army, as in the clear hadiths. So the sign of the Smoke is a divine sign, but it has very important political dimensions; it is what will shape the Dajjal's world, whose duration is a year, a month and a week. Because of this global religious-political change that will take place over a year, a month and a week, our master Isa (peace be upon him) will descend to end this exceptional global political situation, during which the Romans and the Children of Israel will have reached their full peak, completed their full cycle and reached the highest rank in rejecting Islam. Not only by hostility to the true religion, but by imposing falsehood with the power of millions of devils who will be summoned for the battle, for the tribulation and for the emergence, something that has never happened before in human history. So the cause of the Dajjal's rage at the sign of the Smoke is:
🔴 The anger of his allies the Romans at him
🔴 The disappearance of his people's state in the Middle East
🔴 His Roman allies and his people telling him: if you do not come out, we will be finished forever and the whole world will be Islamized
🔴 The rise of a Muslim power (the Islamic world) that will deal with the world with dignity and with other things

Finally: from the Dajjal's contempt and scorn for the word (Smoke) in his exchange with the Prophet ﷺ I understand the following:
🔴 An attempt to show that he will not be affected, and he is a liar
🔴 The scorner scorns because he is angry, which means the Prophet's ﷺ mention of the sign before him angered him and threw him off balance. For the mocker is weak; he mocks because he has nothing but mockery with which to face the danger""")

t(9, 1410, """So it will be like that in Bayt al-Maqdis for 9 years, or seven, or eight; the stronger view in my opinion, and Allah knows best, is that it will be 9 years

So how can one logically and rationally reconcile a hadith graded hasan, saying that the Muslims will remain 9 years in whose era the Ummah becomes mighty and the strongest and richest state arises, with the sign of the Smoke having descended on them before that, the sign that reaps the earth clean, makes it as though it had never flourished and returns it to 500 years ago?
The hadith: (I give you glad tidings of the Mahdi. He will be sent among my Ummah at a time of discord among people and of earthquakes, and he will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with injustice and oppression. The dweller of heaven and the dweller of earth will be pleased with him. He will divide wealth “sihahan”. A man said to him: What is “sihahan”? He said: Equally among the people. He said: And Allah will fill the hearts of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ with contentment, and his justice will encompass them, until he orders a caller to call out: Who has need of wealth? And no one among the people will stand except one man, who says: I do. He will say: Go to the keeper, meaning the treasurer, and tell him that the Mahdi orders you to give me wealth. He will say to him: Scoop it up. Then when he has put it in his lap and brought it out, he regrets it and says: Was I the greediest soul in the Ummah of Muhammad, or did what sufficed them fall short for me? He said: So he returns it, but it is not accepted from him, and he is told: We do not take back anything we have given. So it will be like that for seven years, or eight years, or nine years; then there is no good in living after him, or he said: then there is no good in life after him).
Summary of the hadith scholar's ruling: its chain is hasan
Narrator: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri""")

t(9, 2120, """The sign of the Smoke and mistaken questions in the comments .. What is the difference between a sign of the Smoke before the Mahdi, which produces a paralysed state with no worth, no strength and no industrial resources, and a sign of the Smoke in the last days of the 9 years of his state in Jerusalem, of which it is reported that it is a state in which the Ummah becomes mighty as it never was before? What is the difference?
Many do not understand the Mahdi's state. They think the Mahdi's state is an ordinary state. From here, from this gap, their understanding is breached and manipulated. The Mahdi's state resembles no other state in all the human history we know. It is a state with tasks, not a single task. Among its tasks is to be present, with its leader, for the emergence of the Dajjal, as a mercy from Allah Most High to this Ummah that the Dajjal emerges while the Mahdi is in it. This is something almost no one reflects on, as far as I know; if anyone does reflect on it, that is good and a blessing. At the time of the Dajjal's emergence the Muslims will need a leadership among them that precedes the Dajjal's appearance, to prepare them for his emergence .. People think the Dajjal is just a hologram in the sky and optical tricks .. People do not truly appreciate what the Dajjal's emergence means. They do not grasp with us that the whole Ummah will be gathered in Mecca and Medina in the hundreds of millions, not the tens of millions, so much so that one of the Mothers of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Prophet ﷺ: Will Medina and Mecca have room for all this number? And the Prophet ﷺ told her: Yes. This is among the proofs""")

t(10, 65, """of his ﷺ prophethood, that his Ummah will be huge in number on that day. So let us ask those who talk morning and evening about the annihilation of the Muslims on that day, and who always love to tell us “the annihilation of the Arabs, the annihilation of the Arabs, the annihilation of the Arabs” .. As for Umm Sharik (may Allah be pleased with her), which Arabs did she ask about? The Romans were in Sham, Egypt and North Africa, and the Persians were in Iraq, in the time of the Prophet ﷺ .. So since the sahih hadith in al-Tirmidhi is about the Arabs, Umm Sharik (may Allah be pleased with her) was asking about her own people .. about the Arabs of the Arabian Peninsula, the homeland of the Arabs on that day ..
And if those who rush to conclude that the Ummah, Arab and non-Arab, will be annihilated at the time of the Dajjal and that most of its children will have died and perished are right, then why did Umm Sharik (may Allah be pleased with her) marvel at the numbers? And why the Prophet's ﷺ confirmation to her that the crowds that will flee from the Dajjal to Mecca and Medina are vast and great crowds and not a small number, as is clear to every attentive, alert mind when it reads the hadith that the Arabs on that day are few. The conclusion: the Dajjal emerges in the Mahdi's state, because sheltering these millions in Mecca and Medina will require new infrastructure, new structural measures in the environment of the two holy cities, resources, and food for a year, a month and a week so that no famine occurs. So how is all that to be prepared with pickaxes, which need long decades to build an infrastructure that can hold hundreds of millions, not tens of millions? Indeed even for tens of millions, it is an infrastructure that cannot be reached in 9 or 10 years with the axe and mud!""")

t(10, 820, """The sign of the Smoke and questions in the comments here on the channel
A comment whose author wrote: How can the sign of the Smoke be a punishment and come after the Mahdi; will the Mahdi be punished?
The answer: Understanding becomes hard when a person does not classify things correctly, on the basis of sound thinking and disciplined understanding! The sign of the Smoke is never a punishment, neither for the Mahdi nor for the believing, monotheist Muslims with him, and this wrong notion is what the mistaken understanding of the brother, or sister, who wrote the comment is built on.
The sign of the Smoke is a punishment for the disbelievers and a punishment for the hypocrites who belong to Islam at that time. When the Prophet ﷺ spoke to the Dajjal through the body of Ibn Sayyad, he threatened him with the sign of the Smoke and told him that he ﷺ had hidden it for him. So did the Prophet ﷺ hide something so that his Ummah would be harmed by it? The answer is no. But for understanding not to fall short, the hadiths must be reflected on calmly, rationally and impartially, and the reflection must not rest on championing an opinion. For I receive private messages whose senders say: This is how we grew up and lived .. we grew up with the sign of the Smoke being before the Mahdi .. This is the method of championing an opinion, not the method of seeking the truth .. So the matter becomes “a cow, but it will fly” .. Brother, it is a cow! “Never mind, it will fly” .. Fine .. Whoever seeks the truth will not fall into this predicament .. The Prophet ﷺ stood one day with the boy Ibn Sayyad before him, in his boyhood, and spoke with the Dajjal through the body of Ibn Sayyad, and the Dajjal answered the Prophet ﷺ through the body of Ibn Sayyad. The Prophet ﷺ told the Dajjal that he had something hidden for him, and with that hidden thing the Prophet ﷺ was enraging the Dajjal. When the Dajjal felt the rage, he told the Prophet ﷺ that its name was: “Dukh” .. He did not complete the word (Dukhan, Smoke), in contempt of the sign, belittling it and scorning it, out of disbelief in Allah and failure to revere what Allah intends, because he is a disbeliever. So the Prophet ﷺ became angry and said to him: “Be gone! You will never exceed your rank.” For the Prophet ﷺ could not bear that petty one mocking one of the signs of Allah: instead of pronouncing its name in full (Dukhan) he said (Dukh), making light of the sign. So the Prophet ﷺ had every right to be angry, and we all have every right to be angry at such a thing.

So the Smoke is what the Prophet ﷺ has hidden for the Dajjal at the end of time. Accordingly, the understanding of some Muslims that the sign is a punishment for the Ummah of Islam is an entirely wrong understanding .. Rather it is the inevitable, decreed sign announcing the end of this world, that we may all meet our Lord .. And in it, that is, in the sign, there is no indication that the Mahdi erred in his rule or that the Muslims with him went astray so that the sign descended to punish them along with the other nations .. All this is caused by the mistaken understanding of the meaning of the sign of the Smoke .. which is a torment upon the disbelievers and the ending of a state of the Muslims that will exist in Jerusalem for nine years of ease, wealth, honour and strength, by the text of the hadith with a sahih chain. So how can a hadith with a sahih chain say that the Muslims will be in Jerusalem, prospering in a vast, strong state for 9 years as the Ummah has never prospered, while the sign of the Smoke has descended on them, the crops have died, the livestock have died and the hardship that precedes the Dajjal has begun? What kind of reflection is this?

But those who went in an incorrect direction in understanding the sign of the Smoke supposed it to be a punishment on all the people of the earth .. It is a punishment on the disbelievers by the text of the Book of Allah, our Mighty Lord, in which it says: (“So watch for the day when the sky brings a visible smoke (10) enveloping the people. This is a painful torment (11) Our Lord, remove the torment from us; we are believers”) The Mahdi and the believers with him, that is, most of the Ummah and not necessarily all of it, do not need to say “we are believers”. So the words are on the tongue of the disbelievers, the polytheists and the hypocrites. The matter of the sign of the Smoke will remain stuck in the minds of these brothers and sisters; they will not understand it and will keep saying: No, it is a sign that precedes the Mahdi and it is impossible for it to be after him. Because they will keep supposing it is a punishment on the whole earth, and because they do not connect things to one another. A statement I heard days ago gave me pause: that the sign of the Smoke must come now, because injustice has spread on earth and the people of the earth have deserved the sign!! On what basis does a person decide that the people of the earth have deserved the sign of the Smoke specifically? Why would they not have deserved being swallowed by the earth? Why would they not have deserved the punishment of having security, ease, wealth and comfortable living taken away? All these punishments, and divine punishments are very many. Allah alone is the One who decides which punishment descends on people and on the earth. But for us to assert, speaking in the name of Allah the Mighty, the King, that what is coming is the sign of the Smoke because the people of the earth have transgressed? Glory be to Allah .. Did Pharaoh not transgress? Did the people of Allah's prophet Nuh (peace be upon him) not transgress? Did peoples before not transgress with great transgression? Conceiving of it without asserting is correct as a method of presentation, but it is wrong as a method of inference! Inferring that humanity has transgressed, so the sign of the Smoke specifically is the sign that must descend!!""")

t(11, 195, """The first universality of Islam took 40 years of effort and toil to be achieved, in a time when a man found no great, ruinous hardship in travelling on horseback for months .. The second universality of Islam, under the conditions of the pictures in this post, will need 200 years to come about, not just 40 years, because the bodies of people in this age of ours are not used to the hardship that people endured 1400 years ago. The pictures in the post show the reality of humanity after the sign of the Smoke! The question: if the second universality of Islam will begin after the sign of the Smoke, as channels say, do the images of people's condition in these pictures help one be convinced that these wretched, hungry people, struck by a great shock, can spread Islam in the two Americas, in the farthest reaches of East Asia, in Africa and in Europe?!!""")

t(11, 1530, """A post (its information drawn from artificial intelligence) that may correct the wrong notions spread on some channels about the incorrect belief that the sign of the Smoke is about to occur! What does the sign of the Smoke mean?

It means humanity losing electricity! The sign of the Smoke, which does away with electricity, means the end of everything!

Here artificial intelligence begins to tell us what will happen in the world if electricity goes out forever?

What does humanity losing electricity mean?
1) All the systems of modern life stop
Electricity is not a luxury; it is the backbone of our present existence.
Losing it means the stopping of:
Hospitals
Ventilators
Intensive care rooms
Factories
Water systems
Sewage stations
Cooling and heating systems
Communications
Almost all modern means of transport

📡 2) The collapse of communications and information
Without electricity:
No telephones
No satellites (once the reserve charge runs out)
No radars
No television or radio broadcasting
((((((((((((People become completely isolated))))))))))))""")

t(12, 90, """🏛 3) The complete collapse of the modern state
Modern states are run through:
Databases
Government networks
Financial systems
Defence and security systems
Command and control networks

Without electricity:
Banks will be helpless
Armies partly paralysed
Governments deprived of their tools

💰 4) The collapse of the global economy
Electricity is the basis of:
Money transfers
Factories
Modern international trade
Monetary systems
The making of coins and banknotes

These operations will break down:
Maritime shipping
Supply chains
Factories
Oil and gas
Industrial agriculture

The world returns to the economy of before the year 1800.
🍞 5) A global food crisis
Modern agriculture depends on:
Machines
Water pumps
Refrigeration
Transport
Fertilizers and processing plants

Losing electricity means:
No refrigeration for food
No fast transport
Agricultural factories stop
Stocks spoil
Famine may become global within months.

🚨 6) The collapse of social security
Police forces and patrols depend on:
Communications
Control centres
Technology
Surveillance
Lighting
Fast transport

Without electricity:
Chaos increases
Public order weakens
Theft and looting spread

Security control becomes difficult

🔌 7) The world's return to before the Industrial Revolution
In the absence of electricity:
People return to mechanical tools
Primitive means of living return
((((((((((((Communities depend only on their near surroundings))))))))))))
Most industries die out
The population density of every region falls
Average life expectancy declines greatly""")

t(13, 105, """🧠 The deep summary
Humanity losing electricity = the complete collapse of modern civilization.
For electricity is not merely energy, nor merely light and illumination!
It is the language of the modern world, its bloodstream, its mind, its being and everything in it

Without it we are not just in the dark; we are in an entirely different world that has nothing whatsoever to do with today's world ... the world of the Middle Ages, but with a population that cannot survive by the means of the past because it is not used to that!

My comment: This is what it means for the sign of the Smoke to occur tomorrow, or in months, or in a year .. When it occurs in months or in a year, we would have to forget no small number of hadiths with sahih chains in al-Bukhari, in Muslim and in the other Sahih collections! So do we believe the hadiths with sahih chains that the Prophet ﷺ spoke about the coming future of the world, or do we believe the mistaken human reasonings that herald to us the sign of the Smoke occurring soon? An article for every seeker of what is right and of the correct understanding.""")

